<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45706" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suādus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>persuading</i>, <i>persuasive</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">delenifica et suada facundia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep. 3, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cruor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 453</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">majestas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 11, 272, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conjux,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 1, § 3</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Suāda</span></b> , ae, f.,
			personified, <i>the goddess of Persuasion</i>, the
			Greek <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πειθώ</span>: Suadae medulla
			(Cethegus), Enn. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut. 15, 59</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Sen. 14,
				50</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 12, 2, 3</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Quint. 2,
				15, 4</span></i> (Ann. v. 309 Vahl.).</div>
